{
  "_comment": [
    "Tool-policy fixtures for docs/design/tool-policy-semantics-adr.md (TA-00, konareef#18).",
    "Each case is one manifest shape. 'declared' is [[context.tools]].source (null = no entries),",
    "'allowed' / 'denied' are [directive].tools_allowed / tools_denied (null = key omitted,",
    "[] = key present and empty), and 'commission_tools' is the buyer envelope Tools dimension.",
    "'current' records what the code on main does TODAY. It is not the approved contract.",
    "'relations' records the two candidate subset directions, evaluated byte-for-byte, so that",
    "each option in the ADR can be read against the same inputs.",
    "TA-01 adds an 'approved' block once the owner decides; it must not edit 'current' to match.",
    "TA-01 (konareef#19) added the 'approved' block per case: the tool-policy semantics ADR's decisions D3-D5 as implemented. 'current' is left untouched as the frozen pre-TA-01 record."
  ],
